{title: 192 - O Shepherd Divine}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]O Shepherd divine, I know Thou art mine; Thy search in the night [Bb7]was [Gm/Bb]for [Bb7]me.
[Bb7]This bleak world is [Eb]cold, but warm is Thy fold; My Shepherd, I follow Thee.
[Eb]Thy beautiful [Bb7]lamp shineth bright o'er my [Eb]way,
[Eb]Thy glorious [Ab]light unto Thy [Gm]perfect [Eb]day.
[Eb]Thro' pastures serene, [F7]Thro' valleys [Fm]of green, My Shepherd, [Bb]I follow [Bb7]Thee.

Verse 2:
[Eb]O Shepherd divine, I know Thou [Bb7]art [Gm/Bb]mine;
[Bb7]Thy great [Eb]heart was broken for me.
[Bb7]Thy grace and [Eb]Thy law I picture in awe;
[Eb]They [Bb7]kissed upon Calvary.
[Eb]Ah! life [Bb7]that was given to ransom my [Eb]soul,
[Eb]Ah! heart [Ab]that was broken to make [Gm]sinners [Fm]whole,
[Eb]This world [Ab]is but loss In view [Gm]of [Fm]Thy [Eb]cross,
[Eb]My Shepherd, [Fm]I follow [F7]Thee.

Verse 3:
[Eb]O Shepherd divine, I know Thou [Bb7]art [Gm/Bb]mine;
[Bb7]I hear [Eb]Thee say, "Follow thou Me."
[Bb7]Thy message [Eb]today illumines my way;
[Eb]The [Bb7]Spirit of Prophecy.
[Eb]I thrill [Bb7]at Thy marvelous love to Thy [Eb]sheep,
[Eb]The way [Ab]Thou dost lead to the [Gm]still waters [Eb]deep,
[Eb]One staff [Ab]and one rod, One fold [Gm]and [Fm]one [Eb]God,
[Eb]My Shepherd, [Fm]I follow [F7]Thee.
